 "suggestion": {
  "title": "Suggested route",
  "createdAt": "2026-10-29",
  "basis": "Built by Claude from all 31 places and events in the planner, scheduled or not. Check opening times and road conditions before you go.",
  "intro": "A loop from Santiago east into the Andes foothills, over to the Pacific surf coast, then up to Valparaíso and the Aconcagua valleys. It continues south through the Maule wine country and the quiet coast near Curanipe, and ends back at Santiago airport. Several drives are long, so treat it as an idea to adjust.",
  "notes": [
   {
    "kind": "conflict",
    "text": "Torres del Paine (about 2,000 km south in Patagonia) cannot be reached by a central Chile self-drive. It would need a separate flight trip, so it is left out."
   },
   {
    "kind": "conflict",
    "text": "Creamfields Chile (14-15 Nov) is in Santiago, but on 14 Nov you are at the fixed windsurf event in Matanzas, about 2.5 hours away, and the surrounding days are on the coast. It is left out."
   },
   {
    "kind": "conflict",
    "text": "Cahuil at 07:30 and Navidad at 08:30 on 13 Nov are fixed but roughly an hour apart by road, so you will probably reach Navidad later than 08:30."
   },
   {
    "kind": "tip",
    "text": "Sewell on 7 Nov is a long day: it is south of Santiago and the base at El Ingenio is on the other side of the city. Check in advance whether a guided visit needs to be booked."
   },
   {
    "kind": "tip",
    "text": "Drives on 9 Nov (El Ingenio to Los Andes via Putaendo), 11 Nov (Los Andes to Pichilemu), 17 Nov to 18 Nov (Olmué to Talca) are long, probably around 4 hours or more. Start early and plan stops."
   },
   {
    "kind": "tip",
    "text": "Papudo and Papudo/Zapallar are two entries for the same area, so both are visited on the same day. Parral and Parral: rural Chile are likewise combined on one day."
   },
   {
    "kind": "tip",
    "text": "On the last morning the drive from Curicó to Santiago airport is roughly 2.5 hours. Leave generous time before the 18:05 flight."
   }
  ],
